  // running average and this one is a byte count that must stay exact.
  //
  // `bytesWritten` is LIVE PROGRESS, rewritten by the heartbeat while the dump
  // streams; `sizeBytes` is the final size, written once at completion. They
  // converge on success and deliberately do not on a failure, where the
  // difference is "how far did it get".
